record pattern match on opaque type `YieldCurve` outside its defining module `Shoals.Curves`

Opacity closes the read side too, and that half is not merely tidiness: a
consumer that can destructure a curve can rebuild an unsorted one field by
field from a sorted one, which is the construction route again with an extra
step. `curve_pillars` is the sanctioned reader and returns both pillar tensors
together; `tests/curves_bootstrap.ch` and `tests/curves_bootstrap_schedule.ch`
were moved onto it in the same change, with every assertion unchanged.
